cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TopoConscious in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "TopoConscious: Persistent Homology Pipeline for Neural Correlates of Consciousness"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-09
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Chege-N/TopoConscious"
abstract: "TopoConscious is a Python package that detects neural correlates of consciousness from fMRI/MEG data using persistent homology (H0, H1, H2) of sliding-window point clouds, Wasserstein distance timelines, Müller-Lyer current metric, Gaussian HMM decoding, topological transfer entropy (C++/OpenMP), and cycle localization via GUDHI SimplexTree. Validated on propofol, sleep staging, and disorders of consciousness datasets (AUC > 0.90 vs static FC baseline ~0.75)."
authors:
  - family-names: "Ng'ang'a"
    given-names: "Felix Chege"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-9792-5361"
keywords:
  - persistent homology
  - neural correlates of consciousness
  - fMRI
  - topological data analysis
  - hidden Markov model
  - transfer entropy
  - Müller-Lyer current
  - Wasserstein distance
  - GUDHI
  - Ripser
references:
